{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Sprinkle upon them the waters of the sin-offering.</b> It is impossible to say that this command was given on the day this passage was stated, namely the day the Tabernacle was erected, for the red heifer had not yet been burned — for it is established that on the first of Nisan the Tabernacle was erected, and on the second the heifer was burned. Rather, this is what it says: after the heifer is made, 'sprinkle upon them the waters of the sin-offering.' And even though from the day the Tabernacle was erected they should have needed to purify themselves by means of the waiting period of a day, they were pressed into service for the song (of the Levites); one may answer that they were purified by the anointing oil and by the blood that was on the altar, in the manner of Aaron and his sons, as we say in tractate Yoma: 'water entered in place of blood.'" "<b>Sprinkle upon them the waters of the sin-offering.</b> Since from here onward the duty falls upon them to take down and set up the Tabernacle, they required the sprinkling of the third and seventh day, for it is impossible that they had not become impure through contact with a dead person previously." "<b>And they shall pass a razor over all their flesh.</b> Before the sprinkling of the third and seventh day. Here Rashi explained: I found in the words of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan — because they gave atonement for the firstborn who had worshipped idolatry, and it is called 'sacrifices to the dead,' and the metzora is called 'dead,' therefore they were required to shave like metzoraim, and this is why penitents require immersion and shaving." "<b>And they shall wash their garments.</b> All the more so their flesh, by the rule of corpse-impurity."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase 'שבו ביום' is obscure; read hyper-literally as 'they waited (or sat) a day.' The final quote 'נכנסו מים תחת דם' is rendered literally as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:00.558631713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}